

4) After first login — this is a Simple-AF image
------------------------------------------------
Git trees and Python venvs are already on the card under /opt/fly-simple-af
and are copied into your home on the first boot that has a real user.

Do not install KIAUH on this card.

SSH in as the user you created, then finish printer/probe only:

  ~/pellcorp/installer.sh --install --printer <printer> --probe <probe> [--mount <mount>]

Example: --printer creality-k1m-2023 --probe bltouch --mount Default

Software clones and pip (Moonraker, Fluidd, Mainsail, nginx) should be
skipped. The Klipper *config* step still runs so homing.cfg and macros
are written for your printer — the baked git tree and venv are kept.
Crowsnest is not marked done: the first install runs `make install`
(ustreamer packages). Point cam device at the USB node (often
/dev/video1; /dev/video0 may be the SoC cedrus encoder). Do not compile
uvloop / moonraker-speedups on this 512 MB board.

A USB camera uses Crowsnest. After the installer, edit
~/printer_data/config/crowsnest.conf (device path) and:

  sudo systemctl enable --now crowsnest

Web UIs (bound on first user):

  Fluidd   http://<board-ip>/
  Mainsail http://<board-ip>:4409
  Camera   http://<board-ip>/webcam/?action=stream

Touch UI: GrumpyScreen is preferred and enabled on first user bind
(ARMv7 binary under ~/grumpyscreen). It owns HDMI VT1 after the wizard.
Do not install KlipperScreen on this 512 MB board — X/Mesa apt installs
OOM and have corrupted /boot (uInitrd) in lab runs.

Official grumpyscreen-rpi is ARMv8 and SIGILLs on the H3 — do not replace
the baked binary with that asset. Touch is auto-picked from
/dev/input/by-id/*Fly-LCD* via fly-grumpy-evdev.sh.

Armbian BOOT_LOGO=desktop is kept for the Simple-AF HDMI boot splash
before multi-user / GrumpyScreen.
